 Jay Mehta, Technical Research at JM Financial Services 
Castrol has been consolidating around its 200-day EMA for the last four sessions, accompanied by strong volume participation at these levels. In the latest session, the stock broke out of this consolidation range on robust volume, indicating strong buying interest.
The price is currently trading above its short-term, medium-term, and long-term moving averages, with volumes remaining above average. Momentum and trend indicators are in bullish territory, supporting the possibility of continued upside.
Ramkrishna Forgings, after a strong rally, witnessed some profit booking from the Rs 770 level, declining to Rs 659 in Wednesday’s session. It formed a hammer candlestick pattern near the 50-day EMA, signalling positive buying interest at this support level. The bounce also emerged from a key support zone, highlighted in green on the chart on Thursday.
On the weekly chart, the stock is near its breakout-retest zone, from where the earlier upmove began on strong volume. Momentum and trend indicators remain in bullish territory on the weekly timeframe.
Cyient, after a strong rally, has been consolidating and witnessed profit booking from around the Rs 1,220 level, declining to Rs 1,030. It found support near the 20-day EMA. The price is currently trading above its short-term, medium-term, and long-term moving averages.
The halt in the profit-booking phase has occurred near the earlier breakout-trendline retest zone, suggesting that the correction may be nearing completion and that positive price action could resume from here.
Volume during the retracement remained very low, indicating limited selling pressure, while a strong bounce is possible from this zone. Trend and momentum indicators remain in bullish territory.
