Sapphire Foods India is displaying renewed bullish strength after taking strong support around its 200-period EMA on the hourly chart, where clear consolidation and buying interest were evident. The stock has executed a decisive breakout from a parallel channel on the short-term timeframe, signalling a favourable reversal in momentum.
The breakout is supported by improving volume activity, reflecting active buying participation, while the hourly RSI has bounced back strongly after reversing from oversold levels.
The overall technical setup indicates a positive shift, favouring buying around Rs 233, with Rs 219 acting as the strict risk-control level and Rs 260 as the potential upside objective.
Jindal Saw is demonstrating strong technical strength following a successful retest of its recent ascending breakout zone. The stock has taken strong support near its 50-day EMA, which aligns well with a long-term rising trendline, prompting a clean bullish bounce.
The overall chart structure continues to showcase a sustained sequence of higher highs and higher lows, signalling strong underlying buying pressure and robust structural strength. The setup favours buying around Rs 291, with Rs 274 acting as the strict risk-control level and Rs 320 as the potential upside objective.
Granules India continues to display bullish strength, maintaining a sustained higher-high and higher-low formation across broader timeframes. The stock continues to move within a strong rising EMA structure and recently witnessed a clean rebound after taking support at its 50-day EMA.
Momentum indicators reinforce this positive bias, with the daily RSI positioned at 52.65, demonstrating solid support around its midpoint zone and signalling the potential for further upward expansion.
The overall technical setup favours buying around Rs 870, with Rs 824 as the strict risk-control level and Rs 950 as the potential upside objective.
