 Abakkus runs strictly un-benchmarked portfolios. How does that work in practice, and how has it protected your performance over the years? 
Typically, institutional managers anchor portfolios to benchmark weights, deciding whether to be 8% or 12% in heavy-weight stocks on the Nifty50 because it has a 10% index weight (a practice seen globally with Amazon or SpaceX against the Nasdaq). At Abakkus, our portfolios are completely un-benchmarked. While we provide a benchmark for regulatory compliance, our investment thesis is detached from it. We buy a stock only if we like the underlying business and its valuation, irrespective of index inclusion or index weights.
